SOAPBOX: This was another WQ6X remote-run QRP operation from KN6NBT's QTH in Ramona.
SOAPBOX: Thanks to horrible Space-WX at this location, the King-of-Spain was a challenge
SOAPBOX: from the beginning.  There were PLENTY of SpoTs from all over the world, except
SOAPBOX: Asia (JA's have been playing around in their own GiGs for several weekends now).
SOAPBOX: 15 meters was the BiG disappointment this year.  10 was all but DeaD, except 
SOAPBOX: for the usual wide-open opening to South America, nearly every afternoon.
SOAPBOX: As the contest wore on, the Space-WX situation seemed to improve, while the
SOAPBOX: contest participation itself seemed to thin out.
SOAPBOX: While I heard many Spanish stations, they unfortunately could NoT hear my
SOAPBOX: California QRP signal.  During the evening, 80-Meters was a complete no-show.
SOAPBOX: 
SOAPBOX: Read all about this contest and other events at: http://WQ6X.Blogspot.com
